% Enteral Nutrition: LCD L38955 and its Policy Article A58833 (DME MACs). A
% policy program of the DMEPOS model: it includes dmepos.le (orders,
% delivery, benefit category, continued need, refills) and states when a
% claim for an enteral formula, the pump, a feeding supply allowance, an
% in-line digestive enzyme cartridge or a feeding tube is REASONABLE AND
% NECESSARY:
%   the coverage criteria of every item — the beneficiary requires feedings
%   via an enteral access device to provide sufficient nutrients, has (a) a
%   full or partial non-function or disease of the structures that normally
%   permit food to reach the small bowel or (b) a disease that impairs
%   digestion and/or absorption of an oral diet by the small bowel, and
%   adequate nutrition is not possible by dietary adjustment and/or oral
%   supplements;
%   the formulas: the standard semi-synthetic intact protein formulas
%   (B4150, B4152) on those criteria alone; the special formulas (B4149,
%   B4153, B4154, B4155, B4157, B4161, B4162) when the record says why a
%   standard formula cannot meet the beneficiary's needs;
%   the pump (B9002) when the record justifies it (one of the LCD's examples
%   documented, an administration rate below 100 ml an hour, or otherwise
%   the judgment), and its supply allowance (B4035) likewise;
%   the feeding supply allowances (syringe B4034, pump B4035, gravity B4036,
%   elastomeric control B4148) corresponding to the method of
%   administration, one kind at a time, one a day;
%   the in-line digestive enzyme cartridge (B4105) for exocrine pancreatic
%   insufficiency — a diagnosis of the Article's ICD-10 table
%   (sources/icd10/A58833_icd10_covered.csv, 21 rows, group 1: the LCD's
%   "Group 1 Codes" for B4105, the only group; loaded as the table
%   enteral_icd10) — at most two a day;
%   the feeding tubes: three nasogastric tubes (B4081, B4082, B4083) or one
%   gastrostomy or jejunostomy tube (B4087, B4088) every three months.
% The benefit is the Prosthetic Device benefit (Policy Article A58833,
% Social Security Act §1861(s)(8)), which carries no condition on the place
% of use; the food thickener (B4100) and the electrolyte fluids (B4102,
% B4103) are in scope and in no benefit ("non-covered").
%
% The payment conditions the Article adds (its "statutory payment policy
% requirements" and "POLICY SPECIFIC DOCUMENTATION REQUIREMENTS", section
% remedy): the test of permanence — in the treating practitioner's
% judgment the impairment will be of long and indefinite duration; the
% nutrition not taken by mouth ("Orally administered enteral nutrition
% products, related supplies and equipment will be denied non-covered, no
% benefit"); no stay covered by Part A; a diagnosis code on each claim; and
% the dispensing cap of the LCD's refill paragraph, a one-month quantity at
% a time (the pump is not a supply). The supply allowances are daily
% allowances to which the refill requirements do not apply: a claim for one
% is never marked a refill.
%
% How the criteria are read. What the record states is a scenario fact:
% that the beneficiary requires tube feedings, the impairment (a) or (b) in
% the LCD's words, that oral nutrition is inadequate, the method of
% administration (syringe, pump, gravity, elastomeric control), the
% administration rate, the documented conditions (the shared template "the
% medical record of B documents C": the LCD's examples of a pump's
% justification), the diagnosis code, the stay, the oral use. "Part A" is
% written "hospital insurance" (a capital letter alone would read as a
% variable). Quantities: one supply allowance a day and two cartridges a
% day are read with a month of 31 days; tubes every three months like the
% tracheostomy table (the quantity times the three-month periods begun).
% The findings this policy reads (the judged template of dmepos.le), and the
% criterion each stands for:
%   permanent gastrointestinal impairment (the Article's test of
%   permanence: "there must be documentation to reflect that in the
%   treating practitioner’s judgement, the impairment will be of long and
%   indefinite duration"; parenteral_nutrition.le reads it under the same
%   name);
%   special formula necessary (a special formula: "the beneficiary’s
%   medical records must specify why a standard formula cannot be used to
%   meet the beneficiary’s metabolic needs"; "A diagnosis alone is not
%   sufficient");
%   enteral pump necessary (the pump, when none of the LCD's examples is
%   documented and the rate is not below 100 ml an hour).
%
% Not modelled: the pediatric formulas (B4158, B4159, B4160: neither text
% states their criteria); the additive B4104 ("not separately payable"),
% the IV pole E0776 and the miscellaneous B9998 (unbundling); the units of
% service of a formula against the calories ordered, the DIF of claims
% before 2023, the PDAC Product Classification List, the BA, BO, KX, GA,
% GY and GZ modifiers; self-blenderized formulas and grocery products (no
% code).

the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    % the record
    *a beneficiary* requires feedings via an enteral access device to provide sufficient nutrients; undefined.
    *a beneficiary* has a full or partial nonfunction or disease of the structures normally permitting food to reach the small bowel; undefined.
    *a beneficiary* has a disease impairing digestion or absorption of an oral diet by the small bowel; undefined.
    adequate nutrition of *a beneficiary* is impossible by dietary adjustment or oral supplements; undefined.
    the method of administration of the enteral nutrition of *a beneficiary* is *a method*; undefined.
    the administration rate of the enteral nutrition of *a beneficiary* is *a number* ml per hour; undefined.
    *a beneficiary* takes the enteral nutrition by mouth; undefined.
    % candidate for dmepos.le (read by parenteral_nutrition.le as well, which
    % includes this program)
    *a beneficiary* is in an inpatient stay covered by hospital insurance; undefined.
    % the tables
    ICD10 code *a code* is in group *a group* of article *an article* as *a description* under table enteral_icd10.
    % derived
    *a beneficiary* meets the enteral nutrition coverage criteria.
    *an item* is a justified enteral formula for *a beneficiary*.
    the need for an enteral pump is documented for *a beneficiary*.
    *a condition* is an enteral pump indication.
    the feeding supply allowance for *a method* is *a code*.
    *an item* corresponds to the method of administration.
    *an item* is billed beside another kind of feeding supply allowance.
    the diagnosis code of *a beneficiary* is exocrine pancreatic insufficiency.
    *a claim* is within one enteral supply allowance a day.
    *a claim* is within two enzyme cartridges a day.
    *a claim* is within the usual number of feeding tubes.
    *a claim* is within the dispensing limit for enteral nutrition.

% The Policy Article's ICD-10 table: the Group 1 codes, the diagnoses of
% exocrine pancreatic insufficiency for the enzyme cartridge B4105.
the table enteral_icd10 is loaded from sources/icd10/A58833_icd10_covered.csv, with all matches:
    code | group | article | description

the knowledge base enteral_nutrition includes these resources:
    dmepos.

the knowledge base enteral_nutrition includes:

LCD L38955 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/lcd.aspx?lcdid=38955".
the text of LCD L38955 is at "sources/lcd/L38955.txt".
Policy Article A58833 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/article.aspx?articleid=58833".
the text of Policy Article A58833 is at "sources/article/A58833.txt".

% The LCD's examples of a documented justification of the pump.
reflux is an enteral pump indication,
    as stated in LCD L38955, confer "gravity feeding is not satisfactory due to reflux and/or aspiration".
aspiration is an enteral pump indication,
    as stated in LCD L38955, confer "gravity feeding is not satisfactory due to reflux and/or aspiration".
severe diarrhea is an enteral pump indication,
    as stated in LCD L38955, confer "severe diarrhea".
dumping syndrome is an enteral pump indication,
    as stated in LCD L38955, confer "dumping syndrome".
blood glucose fluctuations is an enteral pump indication,
    as stated in LCD L38955, confer "blood glucose fluctuations".
circulatory overload is an enteral pump indication,
    as stated in LCD L38955, confer "circulatory overload".
gastrostomy tube used for feeding is an enteral pump indication,
    as stated in LCD L38955, confer "gastrostomy/jejunostomy tube used for feeding".
jejunostomy tube used for feeding is an enteral pump indication,
    as stated in LCD L38955, confer "gastrostomy/jejunostomy tube used for feeding".

% The supply allowance of each method of administration, in the LCD's order.
the feeding supply allowance for syringe is "B4034",
    as stated in LCD L38955, confer "The feeding supply allowance (B4034, B4035, B4036, and B4148) must correspond with the method of enteral nutrition administration (syringe, pump, gravity, elastomeric control fed)".
the feeding supply allowance for pump is "B4035",
    as stated in LCD L38955, confer "The feeding supply allowance (B4034, B4035, B4036, and B4148) must correspond with the method of enteral nutrition administration (syringe, pump, gravity, elastomeric control fed)".
the feeding supply allowance for gravity is "B4036",
    as stated in LCD L38955, confer "The feeding supply allowance (B4034, B4035, B4036, and B4148) must correspond with the method of enteral nutrition administration (syringe, pump, gravity, elastomeric control fed)".
the feeding supply allowance for elastomeric control is "B4148",
    as stated in LCD L38955, confer "The feeding supply allowance (B4034, B4035, B4036, and B4148) must correspond with the method of enteral nutrition administration (syringe, pump, gravity, elastomeric control fed)".

% The diagnosis code of the claim, read against the Article's table.
rule enteral_epi_diagnosis with provenance LCD L38955,
        confer "have a diagnosis of Exocrine Pancreatic Insufficiency (EPI) (refer to the Group 1 Codes in the LCD-related Policy Article for applicable diagnoses)":
the diagnosis code of a beneficiary is exocrine pancreatic insufficiency
    if the diagnosis code of the beneficiary is a code
    and ICD10 code the code is in group 1 of article "A58833" as a description under table enteral_icd10.

% The codes this policy decides — outside the section checklist: a claim
% of another policy fails here without failing its own applicability.
% The codes this policy decides, and their benefit: the Prosthetic Device
% benefit (Policy Article A58833), with no condition on the place of use —
% but not the thickener and the electrolyte fluids.
rule enteral_codes with provenance Policy Article A58833,
        confer "Enteral nutrition is covered under the Prosthetic Device benefit (Social Security Act §1861(s)(8))":
the policy for code a code is enteral_nutrition
    if the code is in ["B4149", "B4150", "B4152", "B4153", "B4154", "B4155", "B4157", "B4161", "B4162", "B9002", "B4034", "B4035", "B4036", "B4148", "B4105", "B4081", "B4082", "B4083", "B4087", "B4088", "B4100", "B4102", "B4103"].

section applicability is:

% The codes are listed rather than read through "the policy for code", here
% and in the rules below, so that a program including this one
% (parenteral_nutrition.le) does not try this policy's scope and criteria
% for its own claims — "stage" would blame them. The benefit leaves out:
% "Food thickeners (B4100), baby food, and other regular grocery products
% that can be blenderized and used with the enteral system will be denied
% as non-covered. Electrolyte-containing fluids (B4102 and B4103) are not
% indicated for the maintenance of weight and strength and are therefore
% non-covered, no benefit."
rule enteral_benefit with provenance Policy Article A58833,
        confer "Enteral nutrition is covered under the Prosthetic Device benefit (Social Security Act §1861(s)(8))":
the benefit category of code a code is prosthetic devices
    if the code is in ["B4149", "B4150", "B4152", "B4153", "B4154", "B4155", "B4157", "B4161", "B4162", "B9002", "B4034", "B4035", "B4036", "B4148", "B4105", "B4081", "B4082", "B4083", "B4087", "B4088"].

section question is:

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The coverage criteria of every item.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule enteral_criteria_structures with provenance LCD L38955,
        confer "full or partial non-function or disease of the structures that normally permit food to reach the small bowel":
a beneficiary meets the enteral nutrition coverage criteria
    if the beneficiary requires feedings via an enteral access device to provide sufficient nutrients
    and the beneficiary has a full or partial nonfunction or disease of the structures normally permitting food to reach the small bowel
    and adequate nutrition of the beneficiary is impossible by dietary adjustment or oral supplements.

rule enteral_criteria_digestion with provenance LCD L38955,
        confer "disease that impairs digestion and/or absorption of an oral diet, directly or indirectly, by the small bowel":
a beneficiary meets the enteral nutrition coverage criteria
    if the beneficiary requires feedings via an enteral access device to provide sufficient nutrients
    and the beneficiary has a disease impairing digestion or absorption of an oral diet by the small bowel
    and adequate nutrition of the beneficiary is impossible by dietary adjustment or oral supplements.

% (the third condition of both rules: "Adequate nutrition must not be
% possible by dietary adjustment and/or oral supplements")

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The formulas.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule enteral_formula_claim with provenance LCD L38955,
        confer "Enteral nutrition is covered for a beneficiary who requires feedings via an enteral access device to provide sufficient nutrients to maintain weight and strength commensurate with the beneficiary's overall health status":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["B4149", "B4150", "B4152", "B4153", "B4154", "B4155", "B4157", "B4161", "B4162"]
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary meets the enteral nutrition coverage criteria
    and the item is a justified enteral formula for the beneficiary.

rule enteral_standard_formula with provenance LCD L38955,
        confer "Enteral formulas consisting of semi-synthetic intact protein/protein isolates (B4150 or B4152) are appropriate for the majority of beneficiaries requiring enteral nutrition":
an item is a justified enteral formula for a beneficiary
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["B4150", "B4152"]
    and the item is furnished to the beneficiary.

rule enteral_special_formula with provenance LCD L38955,
        confer "The medical necessity for special enteral formulas (B4149, B4153, B4154, B4155, B4157, B4161, and B4162) must be justified in each beneficiary":
an item is a justified enteral formula for a beneficiary
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["B4149", "B4153", "B4154", "B4155", "B4157", "B4161", "B4162"]
    and the item is furnished to the beneficiary
    and the finding special formula necessary about the beneficiary is established.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The pump and the supply allowances.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule enteral_pump with provenance LCD L38955,
        confer "If a pump (B9002) is ordered, there must be documentation in the beneficiary's medical record to justify its use":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is "B9002"
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary meets the enteral nutrition coverage criteria
    and the need for an enteral pump is documented for the beneficiary.

% one of the LCD's examples in the record; otherwise the rate below 100 ml
% an hour; otherwise the judgment (the examples are "e.g.")
rule enteral_pump_need with provenance LCD L38955,
        confer "e.g., gravity feeding is not satisfactory due to reflux and/or aspiration, severe diarrhea, dumping syndrome, administration rate less than 100 ml/hr, blood glucose fluctuations, circulatory overload, gastrostomy/jejunostomy tube used for feeding":
the need for an enteral pump is documented for a beneficiary
    if the medical record of the beneficiary documents a condition
    and the condition is an enteral pump indication
    otherwise the administration rate of the enteral nutrition of the beneficiary is a number ml per hour
    and the number < 100
    otherwise the finding enteral pump necessary about the beneficiary is established.

rule enteral_supply_allowance with provenance LCD L38955,
        confer "If a feeding supply kit does not correspond with the method in which the enteral nutrition is being administered, then the feeding supply kit will be denied as not reasonable and necessary":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["B4034", "B4036", "B4148"]
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary meets the enteral nutrition coverage criteria
    and the item corresponds to the method of administration
    and it is not the case that
        the item is billed beside another kind of feeding supply allowance
    and the claim is within one enteral supply allowance a day.

rule enteral_pump_supply_allowance with provenance LCD L38955,
        confer "If a pump supply allowance (B4035) is provided and if the medical necessity of the pump is not documented, it will be denied as not reasonable and necessary":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is "B4035"
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary meets the enteral nutrition coverage criteria
    and the need for an enteral pump is documented for the beneficiary
    and the item corresponds to the method of administration
    and it is not the case that
        the item is billed beside another kind of feeding supply allowance
    and the claim is within one enteral supply allowance a day.

rule enteral_allowance_method with provenance LCD L38955,
        confer "The codes for feeding supply allowances (B4034, B4035, B4036, and B4148) are specific to the route of administration":
an item corresponds to the method of administration
    if the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the method of administration of the enteral nutrition of the beneficiary is a method
    and the feeding supply allowance for the method is a code
    and the HCPCS code of the item is the code.

rule enteral_one_kind_of_allowance with provenance LCD L38955,
        confer "Claims for more than one type of kit code delivered on the same date or provided on an ongoing basis will be denied as not reasonable and necessary":
an item is billed beside another kind of feeding supply allowance
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["B4034", "B4035", "B4036", "B4148"]
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and an other item is furnished to the beneficiary
    and the HCPCS code of the other item is an other code
    and the other code is in ["B4034", "B4035", "B4036", "B4148"]
    and the other code is different from the code.

% one unit of service a day, a month read as 31 days
rule enteral_allowance_daily with provenance Policy Article A58833,
        confer "The unit of service (UOS) for the supply allowance (B4034, B4035, B4036, or B4148) is one (1) UOS per day":
a claim is within one enteral supply allowance a day
    if the claim is for a supply of a number months
    and the quantity billed on the claim is an other number
    and a limit is 31 * the number
    and the other number <= the limit.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The enzyme cartridge and the feeding tubes.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule enteral_enzyme_cartridge with provenance LCD L38955,
        confer "In-line digestive enzyme cartridges (B4105) are reasonable and necessary for beneficiaries who: meet the coverage criteria for enteral nutrition; AND, have a diagnosis of Exocrine Pancreatic Insufficiency (EPI)":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is "B4105"
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary meets the enteral nutrition coverage criteria
    and the diagnosis code of the beneficiary is exocrine pancreatic insufficiency
    and the claim is within two enzyme cartridges a day.

rule enteral_enzyme_quantity with provenance LCD L38955,
        confer "More than two in-line digestive enzyme cartridges (B4105) per day will be denied as not reasonable and necessary":
a claim is within two enzyme cartridges a day
    if the claim is for a supply of a number months
    and the quantity billed on the claim is an other number
    and a limit is 2 * 31 * the number
    and the other number <= the limit.

rule enteral_feeding_tube with provenance LCD L38955,
        confer "If the coverage requirements for enteral nutrition are met, medically necessary nutrients, administration supplies, and equipment are covered":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["B4081", "B4082", "B4083", "B4087", "B4088"]
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary meets the enteral nutrition coverage criteria
    and the claim is within the usual number of feeding tubes.

rule enteral_nasogastric_tubes with provenance LCD L38955,
        confer "More than three nasogastric tubes (B4081, B4082, and B4083), or one gastrostomy/jejunostomy tube (B4087 or B4088) every three months is not reasonable and necessary":
a claim is within the usual number of feeding tubes
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["B4081", "B4082", "B4083"]
    and the claim is for a supply of a number months
    and the quantity billed on the claim is an other number
    and a limit is 3 * ceiling(the number / 3)
    and the other number <= the limit.

rule enteral_gastrostomy_tubes with provenance LCD L38955,
        confer "More than three nasogastric tubes (B4081, B4082, and B4083), or one gastrostomy/jejunostomy tube (B4087 or B4088) every three months is not reasonable and necessary":
a claim is within the usual number of feeding tubes
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["B4087", "B4088"]
    and the claim is for a supply of a number months
    and the quantity billed on the claim is an other number
    and a limit is ceiling(the number / 3)
    and the other number <= the limit.

section remedy is:

% The Policy Article's own conditions of payment: the test of permanence,
% not by mouth, not in a stay covered by Part A, the diagnosis code on each
% claim, and the dispensing cap of the LCD's refill paragraph.
rule enteral_documentation with provenance Policy Article A58833,
        confer "In addition, there are specific statutory payment policy requirements, discussed below, that also must be met":
the policy specific documentation requirements are met for a claim
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["B4149", "B4150", "B4152", "B4153", "B4154", "B4155", "B4157", "B4161", "B4162", "B9002", "B4034", "B4035", "B4036", "B4148", "B4105", "B4081", "B4082", "B4083", "B4087", "B4088"]
    and the policy of the claim is enteral_nutrition
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the finding permanent gastrointestinal impairment about the beneficiary is established
    and it is not the case that
        the beneficiary takes the enteral nutrition by mouth
    and it is not the case that
        the beneficiary is in an inpatient stay covered by hospital insurance
    and the diagnosis code of the beneficiary is an other code
    and the claim is within the dispensing limit for enteral nutrition.

% (the permanence: "In order to satisfy the test of permanence, there must
% be documentation to reflect that in the treating practitioner’s
% judgement, the impairment will be of long and indefinite duration"; the
% stay: "No payment from Part B is available when enteral nutrition
% services are furnished to a beneficiary in a stay covered by Part A"; the
% code: "The supplier must enter a diagnosis code corresponding to the
% beneficiary's diagnosis on each claim")

rule enteral_dispensing_limit with provenance LCD L38955,
        confer "Regardless of utilization, a supplier must not dispense more than a 1-month quantity at a time":
a claim is within the dispensing limit for enteral nutrition
    if the claim is for a supply of a number months
    and the number <= 1.

% the pump is equipment, not a supply: a device of this model
rule enteral_pump_not_dispensed:
a claim is within the dispensing limit for enteral nutrition
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is "B9002".
